  "notes": "A Belgian big-room duo, named in the big-room documentation as defining producers of the style — with the same documentation noting that the formulaic construction was itself the subject of critique. That formula is what is authored. The lead is the documented big-room signature, \"a techno-inspired supersaw stating a short repeated figure\", so the melody is the lowest-density lead in this section at 2-5 notes a bar with a high riff contour and \"minimal, repetitive melodies\" over three progression families. The low end is \"one bassline, often aided by one or two highs and lows\" with \"pitched-kick-plus-sub as a single low-end instrument\", so the bass is a kick mirror at 0.97 roots with a single passing tone. The kit is \"a tuned big-room kick with a sub layer, minimal drop percussion, clap on 2&4, 16th hats, and long build-ups with snare rolls and white-noise risers into an electro-style drop\" — 0-1 perc hits a bar, the sparsest in the producer block, against the highest roll frequency. The form is canonical festival: DJ intro, two builds with breaks, drop, breakdown, second drop. ⚠ The research states that all parameters come from the big-room convention; that mark is repeated here, and every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
